> # llama-cpp-rdna-boosts A patch collection that brings **AMD RDNA-specific performance work** to [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp): MTP decode, chunked gated-delta-net prefill, BF16 KV and WMMA flash-attention, fused MoE and k-quant decode paths, a hybrid all-reduce, qwen4exp (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) support, and an attention-memory campaign that frees several GiB of VRAM. It ships as **16 patches** (block 00 + blocks 01-15) for a clean llama.cpp checkout at the fork point **`790cf5 ... (truncated)
Based0.06.003.626 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 4149 (changed = 0), splits = 26, n_same = 6, n_diff = 0
 on the documentation provided, here is a structured summary and guide for using the **llama-cpp-rdna-boosts** patch collection.

### 🚀 Overview
This project provides a collection of **16 patches** (`block 00` + `blocks 01-15`) designed to significantly boost performance on **AMD RDNA3, RDNA3.5, and RDNA4** GPUs within `llama.cpp`. It focuses on optimizing prefill, decode, and memory usage through specialized kernels and architectural fixes.

*   **Target Fork0.08.080.118 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 4149 (changed = 0), splits = 26, n_same = 7, n_diff = 0
 Point:** `790cf51aa` (Re-based 2026-09-13).
*   **Application Method:** Must use `git am` (via `scripts/apply-all.sh`). **Do not** use `git0.09.009.555 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    175, tg =  57.87 t/s, tg_3s =  58.20 t/s
 apply` on the concatenated series.
*   **License:** MIT (same as llama.cpp).

---

### 🎯 Supported Architectures & Benefits
The patches are runtime-selected based on GPU architecture (`gfx1100`, `gfx1150/1151`, `gfx1200/1201`).

| Family | Arch Codes | Example GPUs | Key Benefits |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **RDNA 3** | `gfx1100` | RX 7900 XTX/XT, 7800 XT | Chunked GDN prefill, WMMA Flash-Attention (576-head limit), BF16 KV. |
| **RDNA 3.5** | `gfx1150/1151` | Strix Point/H0.12.018.575 I slot print_timing: id  0 | task 0 | n_gen =    363, tg =  60.17 t/s, tg_3s =  62.48 t/s
alo APUs | WMMA Flash-Attention (3200.12.224.575 I sched_graph_realloc: graph reallocation: nodes = 4149 (changed = 0), splits = 26, n_same = 8, n_diff = 0
-head limit), Dedicated MMVQ tables, Fused MoE support. |
| **RDNA 4** | `gfx1200/1201` | RX 9060/9070 XT | **Highest Benefit.** WMMA Flash-Attention, Chunked GDN, Hybrid All-Reduce, k-quant VDR boosts. |

> **Note:** Most features are back-ported to RDNA3/3.5. The only RDNA4-exclusive feature is **Block 12** (Hybrid HIP All-Reduce), which falls back to RCCL on other architectures.

